{"title":"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/e/e8ec9980ffcb70f01f4a2ee95d1de775637e4e61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2^3 \\times 5 \\times p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"24\" /> is an integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba69e0706e69b8e85802fafc93d0cb6ed9d289f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 5 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 10 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 1 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"406\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the square root to be an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/3/1a383802ab0ae8572c37f43e2f89f8676335e9bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3 \\times 5 \\times p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" /> has to be a perfect square. This happens when the exponents in the prime factorization are all even.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is an integer, this means that the smallest number this can happen for is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56af91b6d706bc17a02d0c8b7f4c0f3f1da9dadc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4 \\times 5^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/feb56b011e8860439521669c0dbe16e6062be2ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 2 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3ad3200f9f47791cdc80ee4cfc4bfe6c37beb5ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 2 \\times 5 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"164\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat\">2006 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160